From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:28:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] RenderManager: release no frame early to the vsync presenter

With more than one vsync per frame, the next picture is released up to
one vsync before its time so the renderer can blend it over the past
frame. The vsync presenter hands that picture straight to the video
plane, which shows it a vsync early. No renderer behind the vsync
presenter draws the past frame.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
@@ -0,7 +0,7 @@
 
     m_playerPort->UpdateRenderBuffers(m_queued.size(), m_discard.size(), m_free.size());
   }
-  else if (!combined && renderPts > (nextFramePts - frametime))
+  else if (!combined && !m_presenting && renderPts > (nextFramePts - frametime))
   {
     m_lateframes = 0;
     m_presentstep = PRESENT_FLIP;
